WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.421
You probably take parts of these
characters with you in some

00:00:04.421 --> 00:00:06.798
ways. So I just want to name
some of your characters.

00:00:06.798 --> 00:00:09.509
Can you tell me what you've
taken from that character that I

00:00:09.509 --> 00:00:12.512
named let's start with Killmonger.

00:00:12.512 --> 00:00:16.391
- Oh yeah.

00:00:16.391 --> 00:00:19.477
That was the one that stuck. I mean, yeah,

00:00:19.477 --> 00:00:21.855
still there it's a,

00:00:22.230 --> 00:00:27.902
I think the unapologetic
nature of doing what he felt

00:00:27.902 --> 00:00:29.529
was right.

00:00:29.529 --> 00:00:31.239
I think there was a,

00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:37.579
a freeing experience to play
Erik that allowed me to dive

00:00:37.579 --> 00:00:43.460
into parts of my personality
that I normally would downplay

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:44.711
or not really.

00:00:44.711 --> 00:00:46.296
- Can you tell me what part?

00:00:49.049 --> 00:00:52.052
- I think it's the
unapologetic nature of it.

00:00:52.052 --> 00:00:55.889
I think there was a certain
level of not giving a fuck

00:00:55.889 --> 00:01:02.145
that he had, that I
kind of had to tap into.

00:01:03.813 --> 00:01:04.481
- Okay.

00:01:04.481 --> 00:01:05.148
I like that.

00:01:05.148 --> 00:01:08.943
I re I remember seeing that
you for a bit went to therapy

00:01:08.943 --> 00:01:10.779
after you were done playing Killmonger

00:01:10.779 --> 00:01:11.863
do you continue to go?

00:01:11.863 --> 00:01:12.697
- I do.

00:01:12.697 --> 00:01:13.531
- Okay.

00:01:13.531 --> 00:01:14.699
I'm a big proponent of therapy.

00:01:14.699 --> 00:01:16.743
I think everyone should
at least try it one. Yeah.

00:01:16.785 --> 00:01:17.869
- Yeah. I think so.

00:01:17.869 --> 00:01:19.621
You know, I think culturally
and generationally,

00:01:19.621 --> 00:01:22.415
that is something that has been
lost within our community a

00:01:22.415 --> 00:01:24.793
little bit or not really
like, you know, grazed over.

00:01:24.793 --> 00:01:30.757
And I, I do think it's helpful
just to unpack a little bit,

00:01:31.508 --> 00:01:32.926
- Just to literally talk.

00:01:32.926 --> 00:01:35.595
- Yeah. 
- Like at its base is just talking,

00:01:35.595 --> 00:01:37.347
which I think everyone,
everyone should do.

00:01:37.347 --> 00:01:40.683
So I'm glad that one of the
things that role led you to do

00:01:40.683 --> 00:01:43.937
was try that. So, so that's
really important for sure.

00:01:43.937 --> 00:01:45.605
Okay, Wallace.

00:01:45.605 --> 00:01:46.439
- Wallace.

00:01:48.483 --> 00:01:49.859
That's wow.

00:01:50.777 --> 00:01:54.781
It's gotta be like a hindsight
perspective from that because

00:01:54.781 --> 00:01:59.410
I was so young that I
wasn't really, you know,

00:02:00.286 --> 00:02:04.874
up until like maybe mid middle
of the season, you know, it,

00:02:05.959 --> 00:02:07.460
I tapped into more

00:02:08.586 --> 00:02:11.464
where I really kind of like
lost myself in a role instead of

00:02:11.464 --> 00:02:14.008
like, feeling like I was acting.

00:02:14.008 --> 00:02:17.428
No, I think there's a little
bit like that felt, you know,

00:02:17.428 --> 00:02:19.514
so, in hindsight,

00:02:19.514 --> 00:02:22.517
to be able to look at the
character and be like,

00:02:22.517 --> 00:02:26.104
what I probably took with
me from that is I guess the

00:02:27.147 --> 00:02:30.942
vulnerability, you know, I
think he was pretty vulnerable.

00:02:30.942 --> 00:02:36.489
- He was and he didn't want
to be in this circumstance.

00:02:36.489 --> 00:02:38.324
- I think he, he,

00:02:38.324 --> 00:02:43.454
he think he felt the
most out of a lot of the

00:02:43.454 --> 00:02:45.957
characters that I've played.
He's probably the most,

00:02:45.957 --> 00:02:50.253
you know, raw and emotional.

00:02:50.253 --> 00:02:51.087
- Okay. Good answer.

00:02:51.087 --> 00:02:52.547
Two more for you.
- Mmhmm.

00:02:52.547 --> 00:02:53.381
- Oscar Grant.

00:02:53.381 --> 00:02:57.302
- Oscar, man.
- "Fruitvale Station."
- Oscar was—yeah.

00:02:57.302 --> 00:02:58.136
Oscar.

00:02:59.637 --> 00:03:03.057
Ooh, that—I mean, that kinda, you know,

00:03:03.057 --> 00:03:09.522
as a whole kicked off a
whole situ—like, movement,

00:03:09.522 --> 00:03:10.398
I felt like.

00:03:13.193 --> 00:03:14.819
It's more like a—

00:03:15.612 --> 00:03:18.156
because it's a real person,
you know? It wasn't like a,

00:03:18.156 --> 00:03:20.950
you know, some fictional
character, you know? Being able

00:03:22.702 --> 00:03:24.746
to spend time with his family, you know,

00:03:24.746 --> 00:03:27.707
and really get to know him
and understand who he was and,

00:03:27.707 --> 00:03:28.541
you know,

00:03:28.541 --> 00:03:31.252
meditating on him and asking,
you know, his spirit to kinda be

00:03:31.252 --> 00:03:34.047
present with me during that
journey. You know,

00:03:34.047 --> 00:03:37.550
it's a tie that's, you know,

00:03:39.135 --> 00:03:42.722
that in the performance,
you know, you wanna,

00:03:43.598 --> 00:03:46.142
you have to play that day out

00:03:46.142 --> 00:03:50.939
like there's gonna be a tomorrow.
- Mm.
- And there's a certain—

00:03:50.939 --> 00:03:53.858
- Wow, I never thought about it like that.
- You know what I'm saying?
There's a certain, like...

00:03:56.069 --> 00:03:58.571
I don't know how this story ends.
- Yeah.

00:03:59.530 --> 00:04:03.785
- So I think what he had to go
through in those moments is

00:04:03.785 --> 00:04:10.875
just the frustration of
being treated like this and

00:04:10.875 --> 00:04:16.589
the constant misunderstandings,
or the, you know,

00:04:16.589 --> 00:04:19.425
desire to just get home.

00:04:19.425 --> 00:04:23.263
"I just wanna go home." Like,
"I just wanna get here."

00:04:23.263 --> 00:04:29.352
So I think that those frustrations
kinda like, you know—

00:04:29.352 --> 00:04:35.775
something that I think was—I
ain't took it with me,

00:04:35.775 --> 00:04:39.237
but it's something that
in hindsight again...

00:04:40.029 --> 00:04:41.406
yeah. Mmhmm.

